## Test Smell Audit — Academic 19-Smell Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `DataAccess.IntegrationTests/UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`  
**Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 (.NET 10)  
**Integration Calibration:** Applied — class is marked `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test (Smell #3)

**Location:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Why it's a smell even in integration tests:** `Thread.Sleep` introduces a hard 3-second wait that is non-deterministic — too short on slow CI, needlessly slow locally. Integration calibration does not exempt this; it adds flakiness risk *and* bloats suite duration.

**Fix:**
```csharp
// Use a polling/retry helper or async wait with timeout
var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
{
    await Task.Delay(100, cts.Token);
}
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky CI failures; 3 s wasted per run even when notification is instant.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic (Smell #1)

**Location:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Why:** The `if/else` means one assertion path is *never* exercised per run. You never know which branch ran without debugging. This creates a hidden testing gap.

**Fix — split into two explicit tests:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — the test always passes but never covers one of the two behavioral branches.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (Smell #4)

**Location:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Why:** No assertion. MSTest reports this as "passed" even if every insert silently fails (e.g., returns without persisting). The test name implies "no errors" intent, but framework exception propagation already guarantees that — the test adds no value beyond what a call to `Insert` already provides.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False pass — if `Insert` degrades to a no-op, this test still shows green.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (Extended Catalog)

**Location:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Why:** 4 assertions, none with a message parameter. When one fails in CI output you see `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>` with no description of *which property* was wrong without reading line numbers.

**Fix — add messages:**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should persist unchanged");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should persist unchanged");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower diagnosis in CI — minor but multiplies across a large suite.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The following tests are well-structured:

| Test | Why it's good |
|------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert, focused assertion on the mutated property |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Clean negative assertion (`Assert.IsNull`) |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count assertion immediately after adding 3 items (self-documenting — *not* a Magic Number) |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Legitimate concurrency integration test with a clear assertion |

The fixture (`[TestInitialize]`) using an in-memory SQLite DB is **not** a Mystery Guest — it's hermetic and self-contained. All tests use both `_connection` and `_repository`, so no General Fixture smell applies.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` after bulk insert | ~1 min |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Split into two focused test methods | ~5 min |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll-with-timeout | ~10 min |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | Add message strings to multi-assert tests | ~3 min |

**Bottom line:** 4 of 8 tests have academic catalog smells. The most urgent fix is the assertion-free test (false confidence), followed by the conditional logic (hidden gap). The remaining 4 tests are clean and follow good integration-test design.
